  <running_head>Hinnulis pernicior. / CANTICI</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Con-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1" type="heading" level="1" caput="3" para="true">ODE III. SPONSA.</l>
    <l n="2" para="true">1. Neque lectulo iacens</l>
    <l n="3">
      <i>Vnicè charum mihi</i>
    </l>
    <l n="4">
      <i>Quæsij,nec repperi.</i>
    </l>
    <l n="5" para="true">2. Ergo sedula statim</l>
    <l n="6">Surgo,pergo,curfito,</l>
    <l n="7">Cuncta viso compita,</l>
    <l n="8">Angiportus peruolo:</l>
    <l n="9">Vnicè charum mihi</l>
    <l n="10">Vrbe tota quaeritans:</l>
    <l n="11">Nec tamen comparuit</l>
    <l n="12">Quem misella quæsij.</l>
    <l n="13" para="true">3. Ciuitatis obuia</l>
    <l n="14">Facta fic custodibus,</l>
    <l n="15">Ecquid,inquam,visus es</l>
    <l n="16">Forte vobis transiens,</l>
    <l n="17">Vnicè quem diligo?</l>
    <l n="18" para="true">4. Nec morata, longi</l>
    <l n="19">Vix ego processeram,</l>
    <l n="20">Quum mihi fit obuius</l>
    <l n="21">Vnicè quem diligo:</l>
    <l n="22">Quem cito iunctissimis</l>
    <l n="23">Detinens complexibus,</l>
    <l n="24">Ipsius duxi meæ</l>
    <l n="25">Matris in conclauia.</l>
    <l n="26" para="true">5. At ego vos,capreis,</l>
    <l n="27">Atque ceruis teftibus,</l>
    <l n="28">Luftra quotquot incolunt</l>
    <l n="29">Additis veto minis,</l>
    <l n="30">O Sionis virgines,</l>
    <l n="31">Vnicè chari mihi</l>
    <l n="32">Hanc quietem rumpere,</l>
    <l n="33">Hófve somnos frangere:</l>
    <l n="34">Donec vltrò iam vigil</l>
    <l n="35">Ipse fese furrigat.</l>
    <l n="36" type="heading" level="3" para="true">SPONSVS.</l>
    <l n="37">6. Ista quænam est aridis</l>
    <l n="38">Prodiens ex fultibus,</l>
    <l n="39">Ceu vaporum surgere</l>
    <l n="40">Nos columnas cernimus?</l>
    <l n="41">Tota spirans thureos,</l>
    <l n="42">Tota spirans myrrheos,</l>
    <l n="43">Atque odores cæteros?</l>
    <l n="44" type="heading" level="3" para="true">SPONSA.</l>
    <l n="45">7. Solomonis en mei</l>
    <l n="46">Hoc cubile iegium,</l>
    <l n="47">Sexies deni simul</l>
    <l n="48">Israëlis milites,</l>
    <l n="49">Milites fortissimi:</l>
    <l n="50">8. Arma docti singuli,</l>
    <l n="51">Ense cincti flammeo</l>
    <l n="52">Præferoces ambiunt,</l>
    <l n="53">Noëte ne quid ingruens</l>
    <l n="54">Dormientem suscitet.</l>
    <l n="55">9. Ille rex idem sibi</l>
    <l n="56">Esse dum struxit cedris</l>
    <l n="57">Monte cæsis Libano:</l>
    <l n="58">10 Hinc &amp; hinc argenteæ</l>
    <l n="59">Quod columnæ fulciunt:</l>
    <l n="60">Strata cuius aureo</l>
    <l n="61">Sunt nitore fulgida:</l>
    <l n="62">Summa cuius obtegit</l>
    <l n="63">Suaue splendens purpura:</l>
    <l n="64">Sculpta cuius intima</l>
    <l n="65">Sunt Sionis virginum</l>
    <l n="66">Inclytis amoribus.</l>
    <l n="67">11. Heus adeste, virgines</l>
    <l n="68">O Sionis inclytæ.</l>
    <l n="69">Solomonis nobile</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Marginal notes at the left edge are cut off and mostly illegible; the first lines are partly cropped. Catchword "Con-" is read as printed.</notes>
</page>
